                                <property name="label">  Choose the folder where to generate modded files.&#x0A;  DLL and Unity Archives are meant to directly replace the game&apos;s corresponding files.&#x0A;  Spreadsheets and Raw Assets are meant to be used in combination with the Memoria Engine Editor (made by Albeoris), by adding the folder with generated files to the field &quot;[Mod] FolderNames&quot; of Memoria.ini.&#x0A;  C# Code Pieces are meant to replace parts of the game&apos;s source code.&#x0A;  Raw Assets may also be imported inside Unity Archives using an archive editor (such as the Unity Assets Viewer available here as a tool).&#x0A;&#x0A;  Older mod files inside the target folder may be deleted in the process. The rules for these deletions are:&#x0A; - If the target folder&apos;s name is &quot;FINAL FANTASY IX&quot;, nothing is deleted (the new files replace the old ones though),&#x0A; - Otherwise, all the files that could be generated using the selected formats are deleted before generating new ones,&#x0A; - The directories are not deleted, which may lead to a bunch of empty folders from previous mod saves; it is up to you to clean them.&#x0A;&#x0A;  Remember to also save your mods as HWS files (&quot;Save Mod&quot;) as these files are more compact and easier to get back to.</property>
