                                            <property name="moveable">1</property>
                                            <property name="name">m_textCtrl28</property>
                                            <property name="pane_border">1</property>
                                            <property name="pane_position"></property>
                                            <property name="pane_size"></property>
                                            <property name="permission">protected</property>
                                            <property name="pin_button">1</property>
                                            <property name="pos"></property>
                                            <property name="resize">Resizable</property>
                                            <property name="show">1</property>
                                            <property name="size"></property>
                                            <property name="style">wxTE_MULTILINE|wxTE_READONLY|wxTE_WORDWRAP</property>
                                            <property name="subclass"></property>
                                            <property name="toolbar_pane">0</property>
                                            <property name="tooltip"></property>
                                            <property name="validator_data_type"></property>
                                            <property name="validator_style">wxFILTER_NONE</property>
                                            <property name="validator_type">wxDefaultValidator</property>
                                            <property name="validator_variable"></property>
                                            <property name="value">PSX version:&#x0A;------------&#x0A;Battle Scene&apos;s models can be exported and replaced by new models. It is, however, not that simple.&#x0A;&#x0A;Exporting a model creates a Wavefront .obj geometry, several Targa .tga textures and a material library .mtl. External programs like Blender can be used to edit those.&#x0A;&#x0A;Importing a model is more complex. I recommand you to follow these steps :&#x0A;1) When you create/edit your model, only use 256x256 textures (merge them if needed ; you&apos;ll be limited to 3 of those textures),&#x0A;2) In Hades Workshop, select the scene you want to replace with your custom model,&#x0A;3) Click on the &quot;Manage Textures&quot; button,&#x0A;4) Browse for a texture your custom model uses,&#x0A;5) Place it at the left of the picture,&#x0A;6) Click on the &quot;Import&quot; button,&#x0A;7) Do steps 4 to 6 for each textures you need, placing them on the middle and on the right of the picture,&#x0A;8) Delete the palettes you don&apos;t use (right-click on them then &quot;Remove&quot;),&#x0A;9) Click on the &quot;Ok&quot; button,&#x0A;10) Edit the textures such as you end up with as many as you use for your custom model, with the right palette associated to the right painting (right-click on them to add or remove some),&#x0A;11) Click on the &quot;Import Battle Scene&quot; button and choose your geometry file .obj,&#x0A;12) Once it is imported, link the model texture&apos;s identifiers to the textures you just set up,&#x0A;13) You are done, congrats !&#x0A;&#x0A;Note that, due to the format limitation, models you import may not be far more bigger than the standart model.&#x0A;&#x0A;Steam version:&#x0A;---------------&#x0A;3D models can be exported using the embedded tool &quot;Unity Assets Viewer&quot;. Most of the 3D models are found in the archive p0data4 but some of them are found in the archive p0data2 (Battle archive) and in the archive p0data3 (World Map archive). The animations are separate assets that can be found mostly in the archive p0data5.</property>
                                            <property name="window_extra_style"></property>
                                            <property name="window_name"></property>
                                            <property name="window_style"></property>
                                        </object>
                                    </object>
                                </object>
                            </object>
                        </object>
