                                            <property name="id">wxID_ANY</property>
                                            <property name="max_size"></property>
                                            <property name="maximize_button">0</property>
                                            <property name="maximum_size"></property>
                                            <property name="maxlength"></property>
                                            <property name="min_size"></property>
                                            <property name="minimize_button">0</property>
                                            <property name="minimum_size"></property>
                                            <property name="moveable">1</property>
                                            <property name="name">m_textCtrl1732</property>
                                            <property name="pane_border">1</property>
                                            <property name="pane_position"></property>
                                            <property name="pane_size"></property>
                                            <property name="permission">protected</property>
                                            <property name="pin_button">1</property>
                                            <property name="pos"></property>
                                            <property name="resize">Resizable</property>
                                            <property name="show">1</property>
                                            <property name="size"></property>
                                            <property name="style">wxTE_MULTILINE|wxTE_READONLY|wxTE_WORDWRAP</property>
                                            <property name="subclass"></property>
                                            <property name="toolbar_pane">0</property>
                                            <property name="tooltip"></property>
                                            <property name="validator_data_type"></property>
                                            <property name="validator_style">wxFILTER_NONE</property>
                                            <property name="validator_type">wxDefaultValidator</property>
                                            <property name="validator_variable"></property>
                                            <property name="value">The following informations apply to the PSX versions only.&#x0A;&#x0A;In this section, you&apos;ll find informations about how modding a game can mess up with your saves.&#x0A;&#x0A;[Memory Card Saves]&#x0A;- Modifying the stats given by the items or the attacks of the weapons matters if you have a character equiped with it. It goes back to normal (to the newest version) when you un-equip then re-equip them.&#x0A;- Modifying the party&apos;s stats, both the &quot;Level Progression&quot; and the individual stats bug. The party&apos;s stats are only used as an initial value so it will have no impact on saved games (at least once the characters have join your team).&#x0A;- Abilities learned are replaced by the new ones and it has the same amount of AP than for the previous one. Let&apos;s say I have a save with Zidane&apos;s Thievery at 80/100 and I modify the game so he needs 200 to learn Flare instead of Thievery, then he will have 80/200 AP for learning flare. Also, you keep gaining AP once you&apos;re done learning an ability (but you can&apos;t see it).&#x0A;- If you modify the Magic Stones requirement of supporting abilities and if a character has it activated when you saved, it will totally mess up with the total amount of magic stones available for that character.&#x0A;&#x0A;[Save States]&#x0A;In addition, for save states, some modifications don&apos;t take effect until they are re-loaded in the RAM (which may be never for some of them).&#x0A;&#x0A;- Spells : the spell datas are loaded at the beginning of each battles or when the player access to his menu.&#x0A;- Commands : the command datas are loaded in the RAM once when the game starts and are never reloaded.&#x0A;- Enemies : the enemy datas and AI are loaded at the beginning of each encounters.&#x0A;- Fields : the script&apos;s field is loaded in the RAM everytime you enter the field. Its text, however, is loaded once when the game needs it and is never reloaded.</property>
                                            <property name="window_extra_style"></property>
                                            <property name="window_name"></property>
                                            <property name="window_style"></property>
                                        </object>
                                    </object>
                                </object>
                            </object>
                        </object>
                    </object>
                </object>
            </object>
        </object>
